{
  "run_id": "PMC12072472__expert_context__web_text_64k_b_o3mini__s2",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Elemental Cr coatings on zirconium-alloy cladding provide good oxidation resistance.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8709257::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cr–Zr interdiffusion occurs at elevated temperatures.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated-temperature Cr–Zr interdiffusion is detrimental to coating integrity and causes premature failure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9318428::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A sub-micron Al interlayer should be applied between the zirconium-alloy substrate and elemental Cr coating.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al interlayer will promote in situ formation of a dense, adherent Al2O3 layer at the Cr–Zr interface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperatures, the buried Al interlayer will rapidly oxidize.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting alumina layer will remain stable and function as an effective diffusion barrier.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alumina barrier will significantly limit chromium and zirconium interdiffusion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limiting Cr–Zr interdiffusion will preserve coating adherence and prevent premature failure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-derived barrier will maintain the protective oxidation resistance of the Cr coating.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to an unmodified elemental Cr coating, the Al-interlayer system will exhibit reduced Cr–Zr interdiffusion.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to an unmodified elemental Cr coating, the Al-interlayer system will exhibit improved adhesion.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to an unmodified elemental Cr coating, the Al-interlayer system will sustain oxidation resistance in both normal and accident regimes.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Normal PWR primary-water operation is represented by long-term exposure at approximately 300°C.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Accident conditions are represented by short-term steam exposure up to approximately 1200°C.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cr coatings can peel and crack during high-temperature steam oxidation.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9318428::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al is relevant to the design of accident-tolerant cladding for high-temperature steam oxidation.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9318428::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    }
  ],
